omx-dsp (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: the header says 0.3.0
  * release: omx-dsp 0.3.0
  * fx/transient: the instance's resolve names its times after the contract's
    controls
  * tools: face-conformance, every instance face takes its kernel's contract
    controls
  * fx/limiter: omx_limiter_instance.h, the instance face, with its oracle at
    every declared rate
  * fx/rotary: omx_rotary_instance.h, the instance face, with its oracle at
    every declared rate
  * fx/pitch: omx_pitch_instance.h, the instance face, with its oracle at
    every declared rate
  * fx/phaser: omx_phaser_instance.h, the instance face, with its oracle at
    every declared rate
  * fx/tremolo: the instance's resolve takes the contract's controls in their
    declared order
  * fx/tremolo: omx_tremolo_instance.h, the host-agnostic instance core, with
    its oracle at every declared rate (openmixer#953)
  * Build against omx-contract 2.0.0
  * ci: no changelog job; git history is the changelog
  * Remove CHANGELOG.md and its CI check; git history is the changelog
  * release: api-docs uploads only on a tag, artifact in the dry run
  * changelog: 0.1.6 was released on 2026-10-07, and the generated changelogs
    are synced
  * changelog: 0.1.7, 0.1.8 and 0.2.0 were released on 2026-10-08
  * CI: use the shared workflows and actions of FreeMixer/.github at v1, not
    main
  * changelogs: the spec's and Debian's generated from CHANGELOG.md
    (changelog.sh sync)
  * 0.2.0: requires omx-contract 1.3.0; CI and release take it from the
    channel
  * The build finds the pinned contract; the checks read it; one more refuses
    a restated name
  * The kernels and tests build against omx-contract's header, not a
    committed copy
  * README: link the project site, not the private openmixer repository
  * contract-agree: an empty gap list is a pass; the gap list is empty
    against omx-contract 1.3.0
  * release: attach the API docs tarball
  * ci: build the API docs on every PR
  * Doxyfile: ignore attributes and static asserts, report every missing doc
  * Document the dyn and gate struct members
  * ci: engine-identity is a desk check
  * ci: the generated limits are compared with omx-contract, not rendered
    from private openmixer
  * ci: every job runs on GitHub's runners

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:58:10 +0000
